{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user has submitted a stitch task (#5132) to create differential tests for `cmd/sponge` covering four specific SRD requirements from srd007-sponge:\n   - **R3.3**: Append mode prepend operation - copy original file content into temp file first, then append stdin buffer\n   - **R4.1**: Passthrough mode - write buffered stdin to stdout when no output filename given\n   - **R4.2**: Passthrough mode with large input (temp file spill) - seek temp file to beginning and copy to stdout\n   - **R4.3**: Passthrough mode with small input (in-memory buffer) - write buffer directly to stdout\n   \n   The deliverable is a single file: `cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go` containing differential tests using the `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` pattern.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Differential testing pattern**: Run Go binary and Homebrew reference binary with identical inputs, compare stdout/stderr/exit code\n   - **testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")**: Compiles the cmd/ package and returns the binary path\n   - **exec.LookPath**: Find reference binary, t.Skip if not found\n   - **testutils.DiffTest struct**: Fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n   - **testutils.RunDiffTests**: Runs each DiffTest as a subtest comparing both binaries\n   - **sponge from moreutils**: Reference binary is `sponge` (moreutils binaries may not use g-prefix, need to verify)\n   - **Passthrough mode**: No filename argument, sponge writes buffered stdin to stdout\n   - **Append mode (-a)**: Prepends existing file content before stdin content in output file\n   - **SIGPIPE handler**: All cmd/ utilities must call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd007-sponge.yaml** (read in full)\n     - Contains all requirements R1-R6 for sponge\n     - R3.3: \"The prepend operation must copy the original file content into the temp file first, then append the stdin buffer to the temp file (sponge.c:352-357). The original file must be read before the temp file is renamed over it.\"\n     - R4.1: \"When no output filename is given, must write the buffered stdin content to stdout after stdin is fully consumed.\"\n     - R4.2: \"In passthrough mode with large input (temp file spill), must seek the temp file to the beginning and copy its content to stdout (sponge.c:403-406).\"\n     - R4.3: \"In passthrough mode with small input (buffer fits in memory), must write the in-memory buffer directly to stdout without creating or reading a temp file (sponge.c:408-411).\"\n     - Non-goals include: no --buffer-size flag, no symlink following, no atomic writes for passthrough mode\n\n   - **cmd/sponge/main.go** (read in full, 373 lines)\n     - Existing implementation with flag parsing (`-a` for append mode)\n     - `run()` dispatches to `runPassthrough()` (no filename) or `runOutput()` (with filename)\n     - `writeToStdout()` handles passthrough: if tmpFile exists, copies from temp file; otherwise writes data buffer directly to stdout\n     - `prependOriginal()` handles append mode: reads original file, combines with stdin data\n     - Uses `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` and signal cleanup handler for temp files\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (read in full, 240 lines)\n     - `DiffTest` struct with fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` runs each test case as a subtest\n     - `runSubtest` runs both binaries in same WorkDir, compares stdout/stderr/exit code\n     - `checkExpectedFiles` verifies file contents after both binaries run\n     - `buildEnv` merges test env with process env, sets LC_ALL=C by default\n     - `ComposeNormalizers` and `TimestampNormalizer` for output normalization\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Key design challenge identified: R4.1-R4.3 (passthrough mode) are straightforward since sponge writes to stdout, so standard DiffTest comparison works.\n   - R3.3 (append mode) is trickier because sponge writes to a file, not stdout. The RunDiffTests harness runs both binaries sequentially in the same WorkDir. For file-writing tests, I'll need to either: (a) write a custom test outside RunDiffTests that runs each binary in its own temp dir and compares file outputs, or (b) use a creative approach within the DiffTest framework. The DiffTest struct has ExpectedFiles but that only checks after both runs complete.\n   - Reference binary name: sponge is from moreutils (not coreutils). Homebrew moreutils installs `sponge` directly (no g-prefix). Need to verify with `exec.LookPath(\"sponge\")`.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive task description containing all project context, SRDs, architecture, coding standards, and the specific task (#5132) to create `cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go` with differential tests for R3.3, R4.1-R4.3.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Instructing me to produce a summary instead of continuing implementation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go` with differential tests covering:\n     - R3.3: Append mode prepend operation tests\n     - R4.1: Passthrough mode (no filename) test\n     - R4.2: Passthrough mode with large input test\n     - R4.3: Passthrough mode with small input test\n   - Verify the file compiles: `go vet ./cmd/sponge/...`\n   - Run tests: `go test ./cmd/sponge/... -count=1`\n   - Ensure all acceptance criteria (AC1-AC4) are met\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (srd007-sponge.yaml, cmd/sponge/main.go, pkg/testutils/difftest.go) and was about to plan and write the `cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go` file. No code has been written yet. I was in the \"Plan approach\" phase of the task, having completed \"Review provided context.\"\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the `cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go` file. Based on the task description: \"Implement srd007-sponge requirement R3.3, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3\" with design decisions:\n   - \"D1: Use the standard differential testing pattern: goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \\\".\\\") for the Go binary, exec.LookPath for the reference binary\"\n   - \"D2: Call t.Skip if the reference binary is not found\"\n   - \"D3: Structure tests as []testutils.DiffTest slices passed to testutils.RunDiffTests\"\n   - \"D4: Check the SRD for the exact reference binary name -- moreutils binaries may or may not use a g-prefix\"\n   \n   The test file should follow the copyright header format, use the differential testing shared protocol pattern, and include test cases for passthrough mode (small input, large input) and append mode. For R4.1-R4.3 (passthrough/stdout tests), use standard RunDiffTests. For R3.3 (file-writing append mode), may need a separate test function that runs each binary in its own temp directory and compares resulting file contents, since RunDiffTests runs both in the same WorkDir sequentially.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5132/c6419ad2-62a1-4d44-aa74-38d7cef3c643.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6419ad